#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# activate

#% text
# `activate(e)` replaces every inert head `inactive(f)` in `e` by `f` and evaluates the result.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `inactive(f)(x, ...)` keeps a call unevaluated; `activate` lets it evaluate.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
activate(inactive(add)(1, 2))
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
e = inactive(mul)(3, inactive(add)(1, 1))
activate(e)
#% output
#= 6

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Without `activate` the call stays:

#% cell
inactive(add)(1, 2)
#% output
#= inactive(add)(1, 2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `inactive`, `composition`, `through`
